<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mavura Mhande</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1629">1629</a>–<a href="/years/1652">1652</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mavura Mhande was a ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> kingdom, installed by the Portuguese in 1629 after they defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nyambo-kapararidze">Nyambo Kapararidze</a>. In return he signed a treaty that made Mutapa a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of Portugal, admitted missionaries and opened the country's gold mines to Portuguese traders. He was baptised a Christian, and his reign marked the height of Portuguese influence over the kingdom.</p></div>
